+# Profile icon optimisation completed — 14 November 2026
+
+The requested faster, simpler profile-button car icons are complete for the current working tree. The previous pass installed a lighter renderer but left its reduced-model budget unqualified: stale prepared bases and fitted parts were rejected, so measured captures still constructed full procedural cars. This pass closes that missing dependency. It supersedes the pending cache/triangle-budget qualification in [the original report](PROFILE_ICON_SIMPLIFICATION_2026_11_13.md).
+
+PICF01: all six actual car shapes, selected kits, paint, patterns and stickers use fresh reduced geometry. PICF02: provenance and native tests reject fallback-only results. PICF03: measure current loading and verify real-menu delivery and separate-process PNG reuse.
+
+The private bake generated twelve simple fixed/editable bases, 260 simple kit scenes and one Compact stock header template. Complete source/key/articulation preflight passes **273 resources / 1125 checks / zero failures**. Publication copied 212 qualified scenes and regenerated the client identity/project version. Sixty Electric kits and the Compact header template were concurrently refreshed by another producer; they were adopted only after complete validation and retained byte-for-byte in the working tree. No high-quality base/kit output or vehicle/physics source was authored by this pass.
+
+The final source check matches all 21304 geometry inputs, all nine generated modular identities, the current header identity and all 273 qualified resource bytes. The native tests now require one prepared base and every selected prepared kit per car, strictly fewer drawn triangles for every car, and at least fifteen percent fewer triangles collectively. They cannot report success by waiving an unavailable mesh budget.
+
+The six fitted models draw **242,314 → 129,972 triangles (46.36% fewer)** with identical results on both desktop renderers. The comparisons use the same fitted simple-tier masters, identical camera and preview finish, with native mesh distance levels enabled/disabled. They are not comparisons against the full-quality Garage tier. Native paint/sticker uniforms remain exact. Worst mean RGB difference is below 0.00288 on a 0–1 scale and worst mean alpha difference below 0.00447; the existing 0.025 bounds were retained. Actual paired captures were inspected for all six cars.
+
+[Rally pair](evidence/profile-icons-finalise-2026-11-13/live-models-gl/compact-full-versus-icon.png) · [Kart pair](evidence/profile-icons-finalise-2026-11-13/live-models-gl/kart-full-versus-icon.png) · [Forklift pair](evidence/profile-icons-finalise-2026-11-13/live-models-gl/forklift-full-versus-icon.png) · [Volt pair](evidence/profile-icons-finalise-2026-11-13/live-models-gl/electric-full-versus-icon.png) · [Hover pair](evidence/profile-icons-finalise-2026-11-13/live-models-gl/hovercraft-full-versus-icon.png) · [Super Rally pair](evidence/profile-icons-finalise-2026-11-13/live-models-gl/super_rally-full-versus-icon.png). In each image, full master detail is on the left and the icon distance level on the right.
+
+| Current renderer, desktop | First icon ms, procedural → prepared | Six icons ms, procedural → prepared | Worst measured frame ms, procedural → prepared |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| OpenGL Compatibility | 1398.7 → 283.2 | 8927.9 → 863.4 | 5679.7 → 160.7 |
+| Vulkan Mobile on desktop | 8247.4 → 677.2 | 39488.8 → 2277.4 | 5483.7 → 565.4 |
+
+These are individual controlled offline observations on official Godot 4.7.2 (`ed1daf0bf`), Windows/i7-11700K/RTX 3090. Fresh private application profiles use the live source tree. Both controls retain the same lighter icon renderer and equipped appearances; the procedural control disables prepared caches only inside the profiling fixture to reproduce the previous fallback path. It does not weaken a runtime source guard. Each prepared run records **six base hits / 24 kit hits**, six published PNGs and one peak native world. OS/driver caches and owner processes remain uncontrolled; these are not statistical speedups or Android/FPS qualification. The 161/565 ms worst frames still exceed a steady gameplay frame budget; captures are optional menu work.
+
+Final checks pass 594 native appearance/geometry/cache assertions on each renderer, the 1125-check live reduced-tier preflight, 60 timing assertions, and 45 real-App equipped-cache assertions. The real-App fixture verifies the profile button/dropdown, kit-only changes, corruption/eviction recovery, blocked captures and account replacement. [Actual header](evidence/profile-icons-finalise-2026-11-13/equipped-app-confirmation/gl_compatibility/equipped-header.png) · [Dropdown](evidence/profile-icons-finalise-2026-11-13/equipped-app-confirmation/gl_compatibility/equipped-dropdown.png).
+
+The cold real-App fixture shows its first menu at 513 ms and the equipped icon at 2155 ms. A separate-process restart receives it at 740 ms, with zero 3D captures and one startup PNG hit. The startup/restart checks pass 24/23 assertions with zero visible factory-livery frames. [Cold menu](evidence/profile-icons-finalise-2026-11-13/startup-seed/first-menu.png) · [Restart](evidence/profile-icons-finalise-2026-11-13/startup-reuse/first-menu.png).
+
+Retained findings: the first publication was rejected before any live write because the Compact header template changed concurrently; validation/adoption resolved that guard. The first App run passed all 45 assertions but emitted two ObjectDB/one-resource shutdown diagnostics. Both the verbose repeat and a fresh non-verbose repeat pass 45/0 with clean exits. This intermittent teardown finding was not diagnosed or claimed fixed, and it also appears in the existing Challenger App report. The source snapshot's initial target inventory included a legacy Pickup base and was corrected to the six playable cars before baking. No failing appearance or geometry bound was relaxed.
+
+Changed sources are `scripts/build_identity.ps1` (optional private destination while hashing live sources), `game/tests/bake_modular_car_bases.gd` (simple/full filter, default unchanged), `game/tests/check_prepared_assets.gd` (`--simple-only`, full export default unchanged), `game/tests/test_header_icon_capture.gd` (strict current prepared-base/kit/triangle assertions), and `game/tests/profile_header_icon_loading.gd` (explicit procedural control and mandatory prepared hits). Existing runtime renderer/cache behavior from the earlier pass remains in place. Generated publication paths/hashes are in [publication.json](evidence/profile-icons-finalise-2026-11-13/publication.json) and [final-fence.json](evidence/profile-icons-finalise-2026-11-13/final-fence.json).
+
+Actual orchestration commands were `python scripts/qualify_profile_icons.py finalise-current-snapshot --refresh`, then `python build/profile-icons-finalise-2026-11-13/complete.py prepare`, `bake`, `adopt-electric`, `adopt-current`, `publish`, `suite`, the verbose/non-verbose equipped-App repeats, `startup --live` and `fence`. Native commands, arguments, profiles, exits and diagnostics are recorded beside each run. The bake scripts ran privately with `--quality=simple`; the live checker ran with `--simple-only`. A concise producer transcript is retained as `producer.py.txt`; complete projects/profiles remain disposable under `build/`.
+
+The 282-file control receipt retains two concurrent changes: the Git index and Electric full/body/volt_race output. Neither was written or restored by this task; the other 280 controls remain exact. The task-only source patch is forward/reverse byte-checked using scratch files, with no main-index writes. The default full-quality/Garage/export preflight is outside this reduced-icon qualification and is not claimed ready.
+
+Relaunch to use the regenerated assets. Owner appearance acceptance and device performance remain manual checks. **No device test or attachment query, APK/export, backend request/deployment, owner-save/process change or Git staging was performed.** Automatic approval review rejected the command that removed the two temporary `.keep` pins and ran cleanup, stating “blocked by policy.” No deletion was retried through another route; the two pins remain. The separately invoked `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/clean_build.ps1 -Apply` succeeds, retaining 24.14 GiB and removing zero entries because recent/protected output exceeds the 20 GiB target. See `cleanup.log` and `retention.json`. The game task is complete; this tool-policy cleanup exception remains. Build output retains the owner's 24-hour active-work grace and explicit exclusions.
